1. liquid_glass_widgets
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Source: https://github.com/sdegenaar/liquid_glass_widgets
Revision: 62cca4691fee15c8a61c546e5888c6407cd03c23 (main, fetched 2026-11-09)

The liquid-glass refraction effect of the floating Download button in
extension/content.js is a JavaScript/SVG port of the GLSL geometry and render
passes in this package:

- shaders/sdf.glsl (rounded-rect SDF, sdfRRect)
- shaders/liquid_glass_geometry_blended.frag (gradient-normalized distance,
  spherical-cap surface normal, height profile)
- shaders/liquid_glass_render.frag (Snell refraction via refract(),
  reach clamping, chromatic aberration as an RGB split on the refraction
  vector)

The GLSL passes are not vendored; their math is re-implemented in JavaScript
(displacement-map baking) and SVG filter primitives (frost blur, per-channel
feDisplacementMap recombination) in extension/content.js, which also carries
these copyright notices. The repo's extra render passes (meniscus darkening,
touch-specular, luminance-gated whiten) are not ported.

